<BaseLayout title="SEO Fanout research examples" description="A synthetic interface example and the publication gate for reviewed provider-exposed SEO fanout research cases." canonicalPath="/beispiele/" pageClass="reference-page">
  <header class="reference-hero"><p class="mono-label">Example register · 31 August 2026</p><h1>See the research view without inventing a provider result.</h1><p>The tool includes one owner-authored synthetic example for interface inspection. It is not a provider observation, benchmark, hidden-query set or search-demand claim.</p></header>
  <section class="case-status"><div><span class="status-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="mono-label">Current evidence state</p><h2>1 synthetic interface example · 0 new public provider cases</h2></div><p>Existing reviewed AI Fanout observations remain published on AI Fanout. SEO Fanout does not duplicate those datasets or present commonly owned material as independent validation.</p></section>
  <article class="reference-section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="mono-label">Synthetic example</p><h2>Which SEO tools suit a small business?</h2></div><div class="case-contract"><ol><li><strong>Input</strong><span>One owner-authored question for demonstrating the interface.</span></li><li><strong>Query set</strong><span>Five synthetic queries covering small-business fit, pricing, beginner use, GDPR and setup.</span></li><li><strong>Visible output</strong><span>Comparison, cost, trust and implementation lenses plus repeated terms.</span></li><li><strong>Evidence limit</strong><span>No provider produced the queries. No source, demand, ranking or content outcome is claimed.</span></li></ol></div><a class="button-link" href="/tool/">Load the example in the tool</a></article>
  <section class="reference-section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="mono-label">Publication gate</p><h2>A real case needs a lawful, reviewed upstream observation.</h2></div><ul><li>Exact input, provider, model, locale, time and protocol version.</li><li>Only query strings and sources exposed by the provider response.</li><li>Source relationships kept at their actual query, action or run scope.</li><li>Rights and retention review before storing or publishing provider output.</li><li>Explicit limits: no consumer-product equivalence, demand, ranking or citation claim.</li></ul><p>Until those conditions are satisfied for a new case, the synthetic example remains the only example generated specifically for this site.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>
